al decision making</article-title><source>Ann Oncol</source><year>2012</year><volume>23</volume><fpage>2479</fpage><lpage>2516</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">23012255</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="ref5"><label>5</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rowe</surname><given-names>G. WG</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The Delphi technique as a forecasting tool: Issues and analysis</article-title><source>Int J Forecast</source><year>1999</year><volume>4</volume><fpage>353</fpage><lpage>375</lpage></element-citation></ref><ref id="ref6"><label>6</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Archampong</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Borowski</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Wille-Jorgensen</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Workload and surgeon&#x02019;s specialty for outcome after colorectal cancer surgery</article-title><source>Cochrane Database Syst Rev</source><year>2012</year><volume>3</volume><fpage>CD005391</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">22419309</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="ref7"><label>7</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rex</surname><given-names>DK</given-names></name><name><surname>Kahi</surname><given-names>CJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Levin</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Guidelines for colonoscopy surveillance after cancer resection: a consensus update by the American Cancer Society and US Multi-Society Task Force on Colorectal Cancer</article-title><source>CA Cancer J Clin</source><year>2006</year><volume>56</volume><fpage>160</fpage><lpage>167</lpage><comment>quiz 185-186</comment><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16737948</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="ref8"><label>8</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Floriani</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Torri</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Rulli</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Performance of imaging modalities in diagnosis of liver metastases from colorectal cancer: a systematic review and meta-analysis</article-title><source>J Magn Reson Imaging</source><year>2010</year><volume>31</volume><fpage>19</fpage><lpage>31</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">20027569</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="ref9"><label>9</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ong</surname><given-names>KO</given-names></name><name><surname>Leen</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Radiological staging of colorectal liver metastases</article-title><source>Surg Oncol</source><year>2007</year><volume>16</volume><fpage>7</fpage><lpage>14</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17499498</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="ref10"><label>10</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kronawitter</surname><given-names>U</given-names></name><name><surname>Kemeny</surname><given-names>NE</given-names></name><name><surname>Heelan</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Evaluation of chest computed tomography in the staging of patients with potentially resectable liver metastases from colorectal carcinoma</article-title><source>Cancer</source><year>1999</year><volume>86</volume><fpage>229</fpage><lpage>235</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10421258</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="ref11"><label>11</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Squillaci</sur